<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
{{> head defaultPageTitle='Untitled'}}
{{> head-component-color}}
  </head>
  {{!-- See solution.hbs for why page-solution is parsed per partial. Step
        pages add the step id and position from the page-solution-step-*
        attributes the solutions-catalog extension sets.

        Shell: the same as default pages (main > .content holds article.doc
        and a sidebar aside), because 02-on-this-page.js builds the TOC from
        headings that are direct .sect children of article.doc. The left nav
        (nav-tree-solution) owns navigation; the right rail is the progress
        card, the on-this-page TOC and the code panel. Below 1281px the rail
        collapses and, on a step page, follows the article (solutions.css). --}}
  <body class="article solution-step{{#with (or page.attributes.role page.role)}} {{{this}}}{{/with}}" data-component="{{page.component.name}}"{{#with (get-header-color page)}} data-component-color="{{{this}}}"{{/with}}{{#with (parse-json page.attributes.solution)}} data-solution-id="{{id}}" data-solution-version="{{version}}" data-solution-status="{{status}}" data-solution-download="{{download}}" data-step-id="{{@root.page.attributes.solution-step-id}}" data-step-index="{{@root.page.attributes.solution-step-index}}" data-solution-step-count="{{@root.page.attributes.solution-step-count}}"{{/with}}>
{{> header}}
<div class="body no-keep-markup">
{{> nav}}
<main class="article solution-step">
  {{> toolbar}}
  <div class="content sol-content">
    <article class="doc sol-doc sol-step-doc">
      {{> breadcrumbs}}
      {{> solution-step-header solution=(parse-json page.attributes.solution)}}
      {{{page.contents}}}
      {{> solution-step-actions solution=(parse-json page.attributes.solution)}}
      {{> feedback-footer}}
      {{> tracking-pixel}}
    </article>
    <aside class="sol-rail">
      <details class="sol-rail-details" data-sol-rail open>
        {{!-- The position belongs in the summary: below 1280px
             28-solution-progress.js closes this details, and a
             collapsed "Progress and code" told the reader nothing
             about where they were. --}}
        {{!-- Below 1281px this summary is the step page's sticky bar: where
              you are, how far through, and the way into the progress card,
              the code, and On this page. --}}
        <summary class="sol-rail-summary"><span class="sol-rail-summary-label">Step {{page.attributes.solution-step-index}} of {{page.attributes.solution-step-count}}</span><span class="sol-bar sol-bar--sm sol-rail-summary-bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="sol-bar-fill" data-sol-progress-fill style="width: 0%"></span></span><span class="sol-rail-summary-meta">Progress, code, contents</span></summary>
        <div class="sol-rail-body">
          {{> solution-progress solution=(parse-json page.attributes.solution)}}
          {{> toc}}
        </div>
      </details>
    </aside>
  </div>
  {{> footer}}
</main>
</div>
{{> chat-panel}}
  </body>
</html>
